From: "Caleb E." <158400752+FoxesRCool1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 17:06:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: romulus13: power the DMICs from vdd-micb

The Surface Laptop 7 13.8"'s digital microphones record nothing usable:
one channel is full-scale noise and the other carries no sound. The VA
macro powers DMICs from its vdd-micb supply (vreg_l1b), but the sound
card routes VA DMIC0 and DMIC1 to the WCD938x's MIC BIAS3 and to
"VA MIC BIAS3", which the VA macro doesn't have. Nothing asks for
vdd-micb, so vreg_l1b stays off while recording and the microphones
run unpowered.

Route both DMICs to vdd-micb and clock them at 2.4 MHz on the 13.8", as
the Surface Pro 11's tree (x1-microsoft-denali.dtsi) does for the same
VA macro, pins and supply. The 15"'s microphones work with the shared
routing, so romulus.dtsi keeps it and the 15"'s tree doesn't change.

Tested on the Surface Laptop 7 13.8" (X1E80100) from a hw-test boot
entry on linux-omarchy 7.3.0-75, with the same routing and clock in
romulus.dtsi: vdd-micb turns on with a capture, DMIC0 and DMIC1 both
carry room sound (correlated between channels), and a 1 kHz tone from
the speakers rises from about 16 to about 1200 in both channels of
PipeWire's "Internal microphones" source, through alsa-ucm-conf's
Surface Laptop 7 profile. DMIC2 and DMIC3 stay silent with their pins
muxed and powered, so the 13.8" has its two microphones on DMIC0 and
DMIC1. The 2.4 MHz clock wasn't tested apart from the supply change.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus13.dts | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus13.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus13.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus13.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus13.dts
@@ -40,6 +40,22 @@
 
 		pinctrl-0 = <&touchscreen_power_en>;
 		pinctrl-names = "default";
+	};
+
+	/*
+	 * The DMICs run from the VA macro's vdd-micb (vreg_l1b), which the
+	 * shared routing to MIC BIAS3 never turns on, so they record noise.
+	 * The 15" keeps that routing, as its microphones work with it.
+	 */
+	sound {
+		audio-routing = "SpkrLeft IN", "WSA WSA_SPK1 OUT",
+				"SpkrRight IN", "WSA WSA_SPK2 OUT",
+				"IN1_HPHL", "HPHL_OUT",
+				"IN2_HPHR", "HPHR_OUT",
+				"AMIC2", "MIC BIAS2",
+				"VA DMIC0", "vdd-micb",
+				"VA DMIC1", "vdd-micb",
+				"TX SWR_INPUT1", "ADC2_OUTPUT";
 	};
 };
 
@@ -149,6 +165,10 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&lpass_vamacro {
+	qcom,dmic-sample-rate = <2400000>;
+};
+
 &spi10 {
 	compatible = "qcom,geni-qspi";
 	dmas = <&gpi_dma1 0 2 QCOM_GPI_QSPI>,
-- 
